//  CATALYST BED 1 of 3 -- an ADIABATIC plug-flow bed on the Dyson & Simon
//  (1968) rate law for an IRON catalyst (constant/reactions; the correlation
//  object is src/unitOperations/reactor/kinetics/AmmoniaSynthesisRate.{H,cpp}).
//  Its inlet temperature is what the FEHE delivers; its outlet temperature and
//  conversion are RESULTS.
//
//  THE VOLUME IS DECLARED, AND IT WAS CHOSEN AGAINST A STATED CRITERION.  The
//  first bed is the hottest: an adiabatic bed fed at ~381 C heats itself as it
//  converts, and run to a 5 K approach it would leave above the 520 C the
//  base data give as the catalyst's limit.  So bed 1 is sized to LEAVE AT
//  515 C, 5 K under that limit -- the run prints its `T_out` and its
//  `approach_K`, read both.  Like the compressor powers, the number was found
//  by running the case (a scan of V_R against T_out), and it moves the day a
//  group changes anything upstream: re-tune it.  Why it is not solved by a
//  DesignSpec, as tutorials/plant/ammoniaStaged04_kinetic solves its bed: a
//  `$variable` in a unit FOLDER does not resolve against the plant's
//  `variables {}` block, so an outer driver cannot reach it (see README).

type      pfr;
operation
{
    V_R          8.72 m3;       // catalyst bed -- chosen so the bed LEAVES at 515 C; see above
    nSteps       400;           // RK4 axial steps
    thermalMode  adiabatic;     // T is a RESULT: the bed heats itself
}
reactions ( ammoniaSynthesis );
boundary  { inlets ( Feed );  outlets ( Out ); }
